>
> I'm a fairly new hacker, and trying to play the game discovering things
> on my own instead of gaining knowledge through spoilers, so decided to
> make a newbie edition of "The N Habits..." thread.
>
> Any experienced hackers have good advice and habits to go by?
> We've all already heard the basics, think before you act, use patience,
> treat your pet nicely, play as a barbarian/valkrie while you're
> learning the basics or for your first ascension, pray when you're in a
> jam, elbereth, etc.

Read the Guidebook and FAQ file.  Learn all of the commands
available - There are single letter and extended-# commands.  Try
out all sorts of commands on all sorts of objects in all sorts of
situations and note differences.  Commands run on more types of
objects than you'd think and act more differently than you'd think.

When you discover some interersting behavior go ahead and try
it on everything type of thing you've ever touched to explore.

Every death should carry a lesson, and that lesson is rarely about
the exact situation at that moment.  Think what happened before.
Did you see a message you didn't understand a few dozen turns
earlier?  Did you make a decision a couple of levels up?  It is very
easy to get into trouble and the lesson is about staying out of that
tye of trouble far more than about getting out of that type of trouble.

Run away, live to fight another turn.  Run upstairs, heal to come
back later.  The monster that dies at a distance can only hit you
with distant attacks so kill them long before they get face to face.

The game is about management and strategy not hoarding and
tactics.  Learn to not carry everything, not advance stuff as soon
as able.

Think quickly, type slowly.  When in a situation take your hands from
the keyboard - Nothing happens while you are not typing but your
brain continues to work.

Every phase of the game has its own puzzles to solve.  Sometimes
the way to solve a puzzle now ends up conflicting with a puzzle
that you'll encounter deeper.  That's okay.  Your goal is to enjoy
the play *now* not to ascend as soon as possible.  If a quarter of
your characters survive even one level deeper yourt progress is
superior.  Don't worry about the later puzzles because by the time
you encounter them you'll know how to handle the earlier stuff in
other ways.



